Z||000002||LarryB||04-24-2000||11:40 PM||||from memory the S-10 series trucks/SUVs didn't offer the FI 2.8 liter until the '86's came out and the 4.3L during the '88 model year, it was the 160HP version.  <P>Sounds like someone did an engine swapout in that Sonoma along the way, I can understand why, the carbureted 2.8 was pretty anemic in the S-10 or Camaro, not much better than the Iron Duke.<P>I've got the 195HP/260 ft-lb Vortec 4.3L in my '95 Blazer, it's a good strong engine.<P>||||reg||1
